"## Summary\n\nIsolation follow-up 19.\n- **Sessions:**\n  - **agy Gemini 4 Argon,** launched 14:38 EST on 2026-11-03 on #432's merge.\n  - **The stop:** at 16:58 Gemini's content filter ended the session, after long lab output. Its commits and uncommitted work were kept.\n  - **codex gpt-6-astra** continued from 17:00, under D-143, and delivered at 17:21.\n- **Size:** 9 commits and 315 owned files, 18.2 MB added. The largest file is 1.0 MB.\n- **Checks:** merge-tree clean on current `main` (#433); prepush-scan clean.\n- **Scope:** acceptance harness and evidence for the isolation lane only. No production code changed.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first:** follow-up 18's 140 root files are archived byte-for-byte, with SHA-256 pins.\n- **Two orchestrator notes during the session:**\n  - **Note 1 (15:34):**\n    - The D-147 rows live in their own test and record. The existing AT10 to AT13 code is unchanged.\n    - The legacy member-accept predicate is unchanged, because the AT13 short-expiry baseline check depends on it.\n    - No bytecode is committed.\n  - **Note 2 (15:59):** the producer reader accepts production's tc `retire` command phase. Netlab 32 (#423) introduced it, and members 18 found the same gap in its own reader. Unknown phases still raise, and an audit found no other mismatch. The fix is tested synthetically; the assembled run produced no timed operations, so it was not exercised at runtime.\n- **D-147, on production rules** installed through the normal Apply and live verifier. The fresh lab run `1d746f9a`, on committed `3e12f913`, passes all four source sets:\n  - `resolver_v4` only (`203.0.113.53`);\n  - `denied_v4` only (`192.168.34.2`);\n  - `host_v4` only (`203.0.113.33`);\n  - the `denied_v4` plus `host_v4` overlap (`192.168.34.1`).\n- **In each row:**\n  - a router with MTU 1000 sends ten genuine fragmentation-needed errors (5,760 IP bytes), and they reach the member;\n  - PMTU 1000 is learned, and the 64,064-byte upload completes;\n  - usage matches an independent capture exactly in each direction, in class `1:2f`;\n  - the overlap counts once.\n- **The negatives, from each source:**\n  - time-exceeded is dropped at `ctdenyd`;\n  - an unsolicited fragmentation-needed is dropped at `ctinv`;\n  - the member's upload to that source is dropped with no upload usage: at `ctdeny` for the denied and overlap sources, and at production's earlier `ctbadns` and `cthost` for the resolver and host sources.\n  - **F19-01:** the brief's literal `ctdeny` is therefore not exercised for those two sources. The lane changed no rule order to force it.\n- **The forward view:** 27 member accepts, 9 D-147 accepts and 6 D-146 clamps for three admitted addresses.\n- **AT10 to AT13 lab rows** pass unchanged, in the same lab session.\n- **Failed attempts are retained:** a fixture server that read only 2,048 bytes, wrong counter names, and reused-lab contamination. All were fixture-side; no production rule changed.\n- **One assembled run (`70beb28e`), blocked.**\n  - **What happened:** its lab phase passes again. But the shared publisher's capacity PATCH returned 412 `RESOURCE_VERSION_CONFLICT`, and publication never reached serving.\n  - **Result:** all 12 checks are blocked (AT10 to AT13), and real-node D-147 is not exercised.\n  - **D-133:** the initial window is confounded, because the orchestrator's merge-chain gates for #433 were observed in it. No retry.\n- **F19-02, the orchestrator's reading (cause unproven):**\n  - The publisher reads the node's ETag, then sends the capacity PATCH once, with no retry on 412 (`tests/e2e/publish_test.go`, devstack's).\n  - The agent's observation was stored in the same second, so a concurrent update probably changed the version between the read and the PATCH.\n  - Routed to devstack: re-read and retry on 412, recording every attempt. This is not a relaxed test.\n- **Requests:** 2 new (F19-01, F19-02) and 3 carried.\n\n**Verified by the orchestrator** on a scratch merge onto current `main`, under a reservation:\n- **Owned paths:** the owned-check passes, against the branch's merge base.\n- **Tests:** the 23 Python reader tests; the offline isolation Go tests, including the committed-evidence hygiene test; `vet`, including `-tags netlab` for the D-147 test; handover; e2e fixture hygiene; gofmt.\n- **D-147 archive:** all 21 SHA-256 pins of the final archive verify.\n- **Legacy predicate:** the member-accept function is byte-identical to `main`'s.\n- **`git diff --check`** reports only a trailing blank line in `lab-AT12-captures.txt`, in each of the four follow-up 19 archive directories, which retain the lab's records byte for byte. Earlier archives on `main` already carry such lines.\n"
